Please review final head 60c5cdaf88e00b5f1d52198317d5c89c5a7a6c2d. The previous report had no numbered findings. Native phase measurements exposed a telemetry error: post-apply preflight was charged to capture. The phase marker now lives in `inspectPaths`, so every real preflight is labeled; the regression fails before this correction and passes afterward. Filesystem work and ordering are unchanged.

Large native comparisons are completing. The prior small-workspace tradeoff remains explicitly recorded; the final performance assessment will include all pairs and allocation evidence before any merge.

1. **Allocate the added regression-test lines:** addressed in `config/test-lines-allocations/pr-193670-authoritative-promisor-fetch.txt:3` with an exact 45-line grant. The native Git regression at `test/scripts/pr-main-refresh.test.ts:968` covers authoritative-source acquisition, omitted blobs, unchanged config/ref/checkpoints, and avoidance of the promisor-history connectivity walk. The shared scalar baseline is unchanged. Against comparison base `d2a166c6ac6399e8940718b8c30fb91615e1c281`, the test-line ratchet now passes (6,494,648 lines; ceiling 6,494,662; slack 14), replacing the reproduced +45-line failure.

The same regression fails on the original owner files and passes on this implementation; all four affected authority-revocation cases pass. Independent Codex review through P3 found no actionable findings. The full changed-file check exposed old main failures whose exact-parent reproduction and introducing/fixing commits are recorded in the PR evidence; no new production change was added during this correction.

